    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">Is blogging still worth it in 2026?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Yes — more than most people realise. Blogging stopped being a diary and became a durable search asset: an article answering a question people keep searching brings readers for years. It's slower than social, but it compounds instead of disappearing, which makes it one of the best long-term assets a small business can build.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How do blogs make money without ads?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">By sending readers to something that earns — your own digital products, or honest affiliate recommendations placed inside genuinely useful articles. The post attracts the right reader through search; the links turn that attention into income, no ad network required.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How often do I need to publish?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Less often than you think, if each article is evergreen and well-targeted. A few strong, lasting articles beat a flood of forgettable ones — because the evergreen ones keep working for years while the timely ones expire. Consistency matters more than frequency.</p>

